# Local-only conversation staging (never source):
# - "Additional Potential Conversations with Specs/" holds _content.json twins of the tracked
#   docs/design-conversations/ set (plus 056, graded "None" and deliberately untracked) — a
#   pre-manifest working copy, kept locally for convenience only.
# - Selected_Chats/ and conversations.json are Conversation Reader staging: raw exports and
#   Cowork round-trip material. The imported truth lives inside the .storyplan files.
/Additional Potential Conversations with Specs/
/Selected_Chats/
/conversations.json

# Derived exports — regenerate on demand, never commit.
# Story data: use the storyplanner MCP server (get_track_definitions,
# list_subjects, list_themes, search_archive). Code: read the code.
# These were deleted 2026-07-28; committing them again reintroduces the
# staleness that caused the v1-Confirmed documentation error.
/TheLionessOfTallTale*.md
/TLTT v2-*.md
/ModelClasses.txt
/Models.txt
/ViewModels.txt
/run_stdout.log
/run_stderr.log

# Saved reference webpages used to seed source-material.v2.json — large HTML
# snapshots (with asset folders), not source, and easily re-saved from the web.
/source_material_references/

# Downloaded source material ingested into sources.db (StoryPlanner.SourceTexts):
# published works in personal-use copies, re-downloadable, and megabytes of prose
# this repo has no business carrying. The ingested truth lives in sources.db, which
# sits beside the .storyplan files outside the repo.
/*.epub
/*.storyplan
/sources.db
/The Princess and the Kaiser*.txt
/Pax Chrysalia*.txt
